<title>JAPAN: HOKKAIDO BANK UP, TAKUSHOKU DOWN ON MERGER REPORT.</title>
<headline>HOKKAIDO BANK UP, TAKUSHOKU DOWN ON MERGER REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Hokkaido Bank Ltd rose and those of Hokkaido Takushoku Bank Ltd fell early on Thursday morning on the Tokyo Stock Exchange after a newspaper report that they were considering delaying a planned merger.</p>
<p>Hokkaido Bank shares were up one yen at 137 and Hokkaido Takushoku shares were down two yen at 115 by 0030 GMT.</p>
<p>Hokkaido Bank president Tsuneo Fujita denied the report in the Japanese business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun. He said his bank plans to merge with Hokkaido Takushoku as scheduled next April.</p>
</text>
